{"evt":"snapshot_stored","id":"followup/bug-fix-acknowledgedaemonrestartonboot-s-cdje","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","subject":"Bug fix: acknowledgeDaemonRestartOnBoot skips not_ready — remove from skip set","description":"Fix a one-line bug in lib/followups.js:acknowledgeDaemonRestartOnBoot.\n\nThe function (line 105-124) has a skip set that bails early if the restart bucket task is not_ready:\n  const skip = new Set(['not_ready', 'done', 'canceled', 'failed']);\n  if (skip.has(st)) return null;\n\nThis means: when the restart task is gated on guidance (not_ready), a real daemon restart does NOT auto-complete it. The task stays stuck indefinitely.\n\nFix: remove 'not_ready' from the skip set. The function should only skip 'done', 'canceled', 'failed' — those are already terminal. A 'not_ready' task that the daemon is about to boot through is exactly the case this function exists for.\n\nAfter the fix, add or update a test in test/ covering the case: acknowledgeDaemonRestartOnBoot on a task with status 'not_ready' should return a result (not null) and set the task to done.\n\nFiles to change:\n- lib/followups.js (one-line change in the skip set)\n- test/ — find the existing test for acknowledgeDaemonRestartOnBoot and add the not_ready case\n\nWorkflow: branch_task → start_task → edit → run tests (npm test or equivalent) → complete_task.","status":"pending","blockedBy":[],"owner":null,"metadata":{"follow_up_of":"followup/harness-daemon-restart","created_by":"daemon"},"snapshotted_at":"2026-06-15T00:55:29.796Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-15T00:55:29.995Z"}
